# Contact form
#
# The form POSTs to /api/contact, a Cloudflare Pages Function that sends the
# message through Resend (see functions/api/contact.ts). Nothing is routed
# through a third-party form service.
#
# These three are set in the Cloudflare dashboard, NOT here - they must never
# reach the browser or the repository:
#   Settings > Functions (or Variables) > add for Production
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY   Secret. From https://resend.com/api-keys
#   CONTACT_TO       Recipient, e.g. nikola@pejdo.com
#   CONTACT_FROM     Verified sender on a domain you own, e.g. web@pejdo.com
#                    Resend requires verifying the domain by DNS first.
#
# Optional: bind a KV namespace named CONTACT_RATELIMIT to cap submissions at
# 5 per IP per hour. Without it the form still works, unthrottled.
#
# The variable below is only needed to point the form at an external provider
# instead of the function. Leave it empty to use /api/contact.
PUBLIC_CONTACT_FORM_ENDPOINT=""

# Google Photos album for /fotos
#
# The slideshow reads a PUBLICLY SHARED Google Photos album at build time.
#   1. Open the album in Google Photos
#   2. Share -> Create link (so "anyone with the link" can view it)
#   3. Paste the link below, then rebuild
#
# Anything the link can reach becomes public on your site - only use albums you
# are happy to publish.
#
# Note: this reads the public share page, not the official API. Google restricted
# the Library API's readonly scope in March 2025, so a static site can no longer
# read albums it did not create, and the Picker API needs a per-visitor sign-in.
# If Google changes the share page, the build logs a warning and /fotos falls
# back to the local photo list in src/pages/fotos.astro.
#
# New uploads appear only after a rebuild.
PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PHOTOS_ALBUM_URL=""
